.TH RUN-CREDCHECK 1 "2026-11-25" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
run-credcheck \- would each lane get past its logins? (the check-in reads the answer)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run\-credcheck
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the credential check of every lane this box runs
.RB ( FLEET_LANES ,
from
.IR $FLEET_CODE/share/lanes.list ):
the fleet-wide
.B cti\-mailer \-\-check
and
.BR "cti\-jira \-\-check" ,
and each lane's own, such as
.BR "cti\-vmscan \-\-check" .
Each makes one or two read-only calls and writes nothing. It writes one line
per check to
.IR $FLEET_HOME/reports/credcheck.txt :
.PP
.nf
lane<TAB>command<TAB>ok|FAIL<TAB>the check's last line
.fi
.PP
The check-in reads that file instead of running the checks itself, so the
lanes' secrets are in this unit
.RB ( cti\-agent\-credcheck.service ),
not in the unit that reads untrusted mail and drives a model.
.PP
A line that contains the value of any credential this unit was given is
withheld whole. The checks print names and counts, never values; this is the
net under that. A lane list naming a command this runner does not know is
refused for that line.
.PP
.B cti\-agent\-credcheck.timer
runs it daily at 05:30, before the digest. The installer turns the timer on
with the check-in's.
.SH OPTIONS
None: it reads the lanes in use from
.B FLEET_LANES
and the checks from the lane list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLEET_LANES
The lanes this box runs; unset, every lane.
.TP
.B CHECKIN_CREDCHECK_TIMEOUT
Seconds each check may take before it is reported as timed out. Default 120.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo cti\-agent run\-credcheck
cat /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/credcheck.txt
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 once the report is written, whatever the checks found: a failed check is
the check-in's to escalate once, not a failed unit that alerts every day. 1
when the lane list is missing, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-checkin (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1),
.BR fleet\-timers (1)
